# .gitignore — this repo.
#
# This is a REFERENCE repo: docs, templates, and scripts, no application code and
# no secrets by construction (scripts/grep-guard.sh enforces that). The list is
# therefore short. The richer, allowlist-shaped file this framework recommends for
# YOUR repo is skeleton/gitignore.template — that one is the teaching artifact;
# this one just keeps local noise out.

# Repo index output — derived, large, churns every build. Never commit.
graphify-out/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
._*
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python bytecode (the scripts here are bash, but contributors run tooling)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local, never-committed secrets — belt and braces; grep-guard is the real gate.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
